Package: croco2atlantis
Type: Package
Title: Convert 'CROCO' Ocean Model Output into 'ATLANTIS' Forcing
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R:
    person("Ricardo", "Cavieses", , "rcavieses@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: R interface to the 'croco2atlantis' Python package, which
    converts output of the 'CROCO' ocean model into the hydrographic
    forcing of the 'ATLANTIS' ecosystem model. It reads 'ATLANTIS' BGM
    geometry, maps 'CROCO' cells to boxes, computes volume-weighted means
    per box and layer and the water transport between boxes. All the
    computation is done in Python through 'reticulate'; this package only
    calls it and returns R data frames and 'sf' objects.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/rcavieses/CROCOtoATLANTIS
BugReports: https://github.com/rcavieses/CROCOtoATLANTIS/issues
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.10) with the 'croco2atlantis' package
    (install it with install_croco2atlantis())
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    reticulate (>= 1.28),
    sf
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
